body:
Clean reconciliation of the recursive-closure repair package onto current main.

Included:
- repaired one-invocation recursive-closure protocol candidate;
- durable discovery capture from the repeated morning audits;
- 14-item recursive-closure validation/integration backlog;
- package index;
- full repair audit documenting four internal self-audit repair passes.

Design status: DESIGN-REPAIRED / VALIDATION-OPEN.

The package now handles:
- audit-generated semantic deltas;
- plural semantic alignment;
- target-observable equivalence and materiality;
- branch/order/confluence variation;
- non-vacuity;
- nontermination;
- cycle/oscillation escalation;
- continuation robustness;
- basis versioning and certificate reset;
- authority separation;
- explicit OPEN/BLOCKED/DIVERGENT outcomes.

Shared live PD registers are intentionally not modified in this PR because active PD writers still own those surfaces. PD-RC-010 records the later reconciliation into PROTOCOL_CURRENT_STATE.md, STATE.yaml, DISCOVERY_REGISTER.md, OPEN_QUESTIONS.md, and FORMAL_RESULT_REGISTER.md.

No canonical goal mutation is included.

Implements the bounded stability fix for canonical ImprovementCore.

- promotes immutable `IC-2026-09-23-002` through the existing selector;
- separates `diagnostic_invariants` from set-valued `successor_set` output;
- defines exact frozen-packet repeatability and convergence semantics;
- adds `tools/improvement_core_stability.py` for packet hashing and invariant comparison;
- hardens ImprovementCore spec validation so future promoted specs cannot omit the stability contract;
- adds a CI self-test for the comparator;
- refreshes the generated PracticalCore runtime manifest for the selector blob change.

No canonical goals, Fick content, or mutation authority are changed.

Uses the new G0 discrimination/integration research to strengthen ImprovementCore.

Validation covers:
- host capture-system architecture;
- cross-layer source/derived/runtime architecture;
- ImprovementCore subsystem architecture;
- Canonical Authority research architecture;
- Fick/Jewish Holiday Booklet product integration;
- PD G0 formal work;
- trivial local repairs.

Surviving changes:
- task-relative non-oracular distinction coverage gate;
- integrated-success gate preventing distributed findings from masquerading as one successor;
- ablation requirement for future capability admission;
- regression cases preserving ceiling, stability, OPEN, and revision-authority controls.

The candidate is promoted through the selector on this branch only; merge makes IC-005 current.

Finalizes the already-selected IC-005 semantic successor after cross-domain validation.

- marks IC-005 canonical semantic current and repins its exact blob;
- records propagation to system/cross-layer architecture, Canonical Authority, JHB/Fick, and G0;
- drains the broad temporary conversation item;
- retains only the unvalidated AuditCore transfer as a narrower Sort Later candidate.

No AuditCore promotion is claimed.

Tests the user's connection-audit idea as a ceiling generator and separately propagates what IC-005 taught us about the non-PD validation targets.

Bridge validation distinguishes:
- genuine two-sided synthesis (G0 x ImprovementCore; distinction coverage x ablation);
- ordinary transfer (PD -> Canonical Authority);
- existing architecture analysis (goal spine x layered control);
- open/non-demonstrated bridges (Fick science x Jewish concept);
- unrelated-pair rejection.

The surviving change is bounded bridge synthesis as a selectable ceiling generator, not a mandatory stage. Arbitrary pair search is prohibited. IC-006 remains semantically compatible with PCO-002.

Also records substantive findings about capture architecture, cross-layer composition, Canonical Authority manuscript integration, and Fick booklet-level integration.

Runs a wide, bounded cross-project scan centered on the fixed requirement that is/ought remain load-bearing in the REBT paper.

Methods applied: IC-006 Bridge synthesis, TransferCore logic, HF-001 dependency analysis, orthogonal decomposition, PD attribution/anti-supplementation, information-loss/OPEN, distinction/integration, drift, MRAC, hostile tests, and ceiling challenge.

Strongest gains:
- typed bridge premises by role (descriptive, normative, constitutive, authority, pragmatic, classificatory);
- valid augmented inference vs source-contained inference;
- an application contract for is/ought attribution itself;
- a new integration question for REBT rationality criteria;
- domain-crossing licensing edges as a broader comparator family while keeping Hume indispensable;
- strong transfers to psychological-distress, canonical-authority, gender-norms, emotion, and measurement work.

The scan rejects collapsing every REBT irrational belief into an is/ought fallacy and preserves is/ought as the anchor/theoretical engine.
